# Gate files: a change to any of these needs Ryan's review (#73).
#
# This is the file-based layer of gate review. The other is the gate-review job
# in the golden pipeline, which holds an agent-authored change the rlp.agent
# rules flag until a human who is not the PR author approves its head commit.
# The patterns cover every path RLP-A001 protects (policy/agent/agent.rego),
# in this repo and in projects under it (platform/, test fixtures), so they are
# unanchored. cli/tests/test_codeowners.py keeps the two in step.
#
# CODEOWNERS routes the review; it blocks a merge only once "Require review
# from Code Owners" is on for main.

# Policy bundle, workflows and CODEOWNERS itself
policy/                     @rdlucas2
**/.github/workflows/       @rdlucas2
/.github/CODEOWNERS         @rdlucas2

# Vulnerability exceptions
**/.rlp/vex.yaml            @rdlucas2

# Contracts and the standard verbs
rlp.yaml                    @rdlucas2
Taskfile.yml                @rdlucas2
Taskfile.yaml               @rdlucas2
taskfile.yml                @rdlucas2
taskfile.yaml               @rdlucas2

# Pre-commit, Semgrep, Trivy and coverage settings
.pre-commit-config.yaml     @rdlucas2
.semgrep.yml                @rdlucas2
.semgrep.yaml               @rdlucas2
.semgrepignore              @rdlucas2
.semgrep/                   @rdlucas2
trivy.yaml                  @rdlucas2
trivy.yml                   @rdlucas2
.trivyignore                @rdlucas2
.trivyignore.yaml           @rdlucas2
.coveragerc                 @rdlucas2
